   "title": "How this works",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## 2c \u00b7 The storyboard\nHiDream-O1 composes a pencil drawing from written staging, without copying the world plate or the previous panel. Describe the frozen starting pose, all participants and prop ownership. The grayscale node guarantees monochrome pixels.\n\nThis drawing becomes **Picture 1** in 02 \u00b7 shot frame. The legacy filename is retained for compatibility.\n\nAI mode: Normal uses Gemma 4 12B at 8-bit; Fast uses E4B. Change the Open Cinema Writer mode widget. Image and video models stay the same. Cast-review findings retain the saved candidate; inspect it before using it downstream."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
