   "title": "Staging, cast, location and framing",
   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "CLIPTextEncode"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "One uninterrupted monochrome pencil storyboard image, a single camera view. Exactly 1 visible characters, each appearing once. Empty background with no other figures or bystanders. Stage this exact opening moment: He holds the lens up to the sun on the glass terrace; the city drifts behind him. The scene action for context, not its later outcome: He holds the lens up to the sun on the glass terrace; the city drifts behind him. Preserve the specified viewing angle and eyelines. Show the participants engaged in the action, not lined up for a portrait. Camera framing: medium close-up from the chest up. Readable acting poses and separated silhouettes; the characters interact with the scene, not the viewer. Lead wardrobe and appearance within this crop: Slender build, early twenties, sharp cheekbones framed by dark, tightly braided hair. He wears a tunic of deep indigo linen cinched with a leather sash. He clutches a delicate, glowing crucible. Continuity: Thin build, indigo linen, dark braids, glowing crucible. Indicate only the location named in the staging with sparse pencil marks; leave all other space white. Tight crop: the subject fills the frame and extends beyond its edges; no full body or whole building. Exactly 1 visible characters, each appearing once. Empty background with no other figures or bystanders. All named colours are grey values in this drawing. Black, grey and white only. One panel edge to edge, no lettering, borders or drawing equipment."
   ]
  },
